+---
+
+# Attribution: allowed English word set (`vocab-allowed.ts`)
+
+`vocab-allowed.ts` is an adapted work of the **FrequencyWords** English frequency list. It is
+the shared word set used by `frame.dte = "bb-k-v4s"` (pack `fw50k-all-d1-gf`).
+
+- **Work**: FrequencyWords, file `content/2018/en/en_50k.txt`
+- **Author**: Hermit Dave (GitHub: `hermitdave`)
+- **Source URL**: https://github.com/hermitdave/FrequencyWords
+- **Upstream corpus**: OpenSubtitles 2018 via OPUS (http://opus.nlpl.eu/OpenSubtitles2018.php)
+- **License of the word-list content**: Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0
+  International (CC BY-SA 4.0), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
+  The full license text is in `vocab-en.LICENSE.txt` next to this file.
+  (The FrequencyWords *code* is MIT; no FrequencyWords code is used here, only data.)
+
+## Modifications made (CC BY-SA 4.0 section 3(a)(1)(B))
+1. Kept only tokens matching `[a-z]+` (dropped digits, punctuation, apostrophes, non-ASCII).
+2. Removed duplicates, keeping the first (highest-count) occurrence.
+3. Removed a small set of specified whole words at build time (the list is a build input and
+   is not distributed).
+4. Kept the top 32,768 remaining tokens by occurrence count, with their counts.
+5. Packed the words and counts into a TypeScript module (`vocab-allowed.ts`), generated by
+   `scripts/build-vocab-allowed.mjs`.
+6. At run time the words are re-ordered within near-equal-frequency rank groups by a
+   per-session key; the counts are used as the frequency table.
+
+Compared with the upstream file, the removed words can be recovered by anyone; the list is
+not secret.
+
+## ShareAlike
+This adapted word list is licensed under **CC BY-SA 4.0**, the same license. ShareAlike
+applies to the adapted word-list data (`vocab-allowed.ts`) and to any further adaptation of
+it. It does not by itself relicense the rest of this repository. Because the list is bundled
+into `public/agent/lexis-frame.mjs`, a copy of this notice is included in
+`public/agent/NOTICE-vocab.txt`.
+
+No endorsement by the author or by Creative Commons is implied. Provided "as is",
+without warranties (see license section 5).
